@startuml
title Multithreaded Data Acquisition Pipeline - Read Side Component Diagram

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "CLI User" as User
component "Pipeline CLI\n(command-line executable)" as CLI
component "ioPipelineController" as Controller
component "ioUsbReadController\n<<read worker>>" as ReadWorker
queue "ioDataBuffer\n<<circular buffer>>" as CircularBuffer

interface "ioReadableByteStream\n<<input source protocol>>" as InputSource
component "ioFileInputByteStream\n<<file input source>>" as FileInput
component "ioFtdiByteStream\n<<FTDI input source>>" as FtdiInput

component "InputSession : ioFtdiSession\n<<existing>>" as InputSession
node "FTDI Input Device" as InputDevice
file "Input File" as InputFile

User --> CLI : run pipeline or compare-files
CLI --> Controller : configure / create / start / stop

Controller --> ReadWorker : manage thread lifecycle
Controller --> CircularBuffer : create / close
Controller --> InputSource : select implementation

ReadWorker --> InputSource : read from source
InputSource --> FileInput : file mode
InputSource --> FtdiInput : FTDI mode
FileInput --> InputFile : read bytes / EOF
FtdiInput --> InputSession : FTDI session calls
InputSession --> InputDevice : FT_Read operations

ReadWorker --> CircularBuffer : push byte chunks

note right of ReadWorker
ReadWorker.
Current input path can be either
FTDI hardware or a file-based demo source.
end note

note bottom of CircularBuffer
Primary producer-consumer handoff.
Implemented as ioDataBuffer with
bounded ring storage and blocking
push and pop synchronization.
end note

note bottom of CLI
The repo now includes a compare-files
subcommand for byte-for-byte validation
of demo and reference binaries.
end note
@enduml